  "result": "I found the cause and wrote up a fix, but haven't applied it because plan mode is active.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options()` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts a parameter's option names by prefix length with `reverse=True`. That puts long names first, so `--help, -h` appears instead of `-h, --help`. The existing tests in `tests/test_commands.py:188-190` expect the short name first.\n\n**Fix:** change line 319 to:\n\n```python\nrv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n```\n\n**Verification:** run `pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_formatting.py tests/test_options.py`, then the full suite, and check `--help` on one of the examples.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-resilient-kitten.md`. The plan-approval tool wasn't available in this session, so tell me to go ahead if you'd like me to apply it.",
